/// StallingClient — an `HTTPClient` stand-in whose request takes 2 s
/// whatever `#timeout` it is given, as a response that trickles in a few
/// bytes at a time does (`HTTPClient`'s timeout bounds each read, not the
/// whole response). Tests hand it to the HTTP adapter as its `client` to
/// show the deadline cuts the request off regardless.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// StallingClient stallMs   // => 2000
/// ```
Object subclass: StallingClient

  /// How long each request takes, in milliseconds.
  class stallMs -> Integer => 2000

  /// The `HTTPClient` request protocol: wait, then answer an error.
  class request: _method :: Object url: _url :: Object options: _opts :: Dictionary -> Result =>
    Erlang timer sleep: self stallMs
    Result error: "stalled"
